### Phase 1 evidence

- Added `tests/automation/support/command_conformance.lua` as test-only support.
  It validates complete host capability declarations, rejects unknown fields
  and pointer, input, redraw, or viewport contradictions, and supplies shared
  exact-root, redraw-generation, pointer/button restoration, bounded tree and
  screen capture, observation-counter, and failure-safe cleanup assertions.
  It contains no mount construction, native callback invocation, or production
  behavior.
- Ordinary-widget, overlay-widget, and complete-screen specifications each
  retain their own concrete DFHack class, backing-screen, and `ds.mount()`
  setup. All three declare their capabilities locally and use the shared
  exact-mounted-root assertion, removing repeated raw identity assertions
  without obscuring the real host or interaction target.
- `.\tools\Run-UnitTests.ps1 --filter "command conformance support"` passed
  6 successes, 0 failures, 0 errors, and 0 pending. The focused cases prove
  unknown, incomplete, and contradictory capability rejection; cleanup after
  success; cleanup continuation after simultaneous injected body and cleanup
  failures; retained-ownership detection; redraw timing; bounded captures;
  counters; and exact pointer/button comparison.
- Focused live specifications ran sequentially. Ordinary widget passed
  4 successes, overlay widget passed 4 successes, and complete screen passed
  2 successes. Every run reported 0 failures, 0 errors, 0 pending, and
  `cleanup_confirmed=true`.
- `.\tools\Run-AutomationTests.ps1` passed 31 successes, 0 failures, 0 errors,
  and 0 pending with `FINISHED passed cleanup_confirmed=true`.
  `.\tools\Run-UnitTests.ps1` passed 450 successes, 0 failures, 0 errors, and
  0 pending. `.\tools\Check-Lua.ps1` passed Lua 5.4.6 syntax and formatting
  checks for 234 files.
- Final process evidence found responsive Dwarf Fortress PID 36940 at
  `G:\Steam\steamapps\common\Dwarf Fortress\Dwarf Fortress.exe`.
  The core-context probe reported protocol 2, `core=true`, and timeout support.
  `lua bin\dwarfspec status` reported the executor idle, queue depth 0, and no
  quarantine.
- `git diff --check` and `git diff --cached --check` passed. Worktree changes
  are limited to this checklist, the new test-only helper and focused unit
  specification, and the three mount-host specifications that consume the
  shared identity assertion.

### Phase 2 evidence

- Extended `tests/automation/ordinary_widget_mount_live_spec.lua` with a
  rendered `pointer_target` and test-owned ordinary-host observations for
  keyboard input, physical click/down/up, wheel handling, pointer-over-render
  checks, and completed renders. All observations are reached through public
  DwarfSpec commands and the normal `gui.ZScreen`/widget input path.
- Root-default `ds.inspect()` proves exact mounted-root identity, view ID,
  visibility, activity, and live body bounds. Top-level and fluent forms of
  click, hover, input, type, and pointer placement each produce matching
  observable counter, text, render, or coordinate changes. The fluent focus
  list is nonempty, bounded to eight entries, contains only nonempty strings,
  and identifies the DwarfSpec component host.
- Every physical action first calls `target:hover()` and asserts the pointer is
  inside the rendered target. Default left click is observed. DOWN and UP
  prove the temporary `mouse_lbut_down`/`mouse_lbut_lift`, `mouse_focus`, and
  `tracking_on` fields during dispatch, their post-UP reset, and exact
  pointer/button snapshot restoration after unmount. Scroll-down is explicitly
  handled and counted by the ordinary host.
- Shared redraw assertions prove top-level default redraw returns after a newer
  render and `{wait=false}` returns at the current generation before a bounded
  `ds.await()` observes the later render. The teardown case deliberately leaves
  a DOWN claim active before unmount, then proves exact pointer/button, native
  window, pause, backing screen, instance render/resize method, subject,
  owned-screen, map-view, and render-observer restoration.
- The focused command
  `.\tools\Run-AutomationTests.ps1 --test-glob
  tests/automation/ordinary_widget_mount_live_spec.lua` passed 7 successes,
  0 failures, 0 errors, and 0 pending with
  `FINISHED passed cleanup_confirmed=true`.
- The first broad attempt coincided with a Dwarf Fortress restart and was
